" Tridactyl reads this file at Firefox startup. Run :source after editing it.

" Drop settings made in the browser, so this file is the whole config.
sanitise tridactyllocal tridactylsync

" Start every page in ignore mode: Firefox keeps its own keys and Tridactyl
" only answers to the bindings below. Delete this line for Tridactyl's Vim keys.
autocmd DocStart .* mode ignore

" Ctrl+Space is the prefix key. A plain <C-Space>j fails when Ctrl is released
" before Space, because that Space release arrives without Ctrl. The prefix is
" written as: Ctrl+Space pressed, then an optional Space release with or
" without Ctrl. `bind` would drop the optional releases, so `set` writes the
" key maps directly.
" Each sequence is set in every mode a page can be in, so it also works while
" typing in a text field.
set ignoremaps.<CD-Space><?CU-Space><?U-Space>j tabnext
set ignoremaps.<CD-Space><?CU-Space><?U-Space>k tabprev
set nmaps.<CD-Space><?CU-Space><?U-Space>j tabnext
set nmaps.<CD-Space><?CU-Space><?U-Space>k tabprev
set imaps.<CD-Space><?CU-Space><?U-Space>j tabnext
set imaps.<CD-Space><?CU-Space><?U-Space>k tabprev
set inputmaps.<CD-Space><?CU-Space><?U-Space>j tabnext
set inputmaps.<CD-Space><?CU-Space><?U-Space>k tabprev
